            "title": "CME Group Shares Steady After Hours-Long Trading Outage",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "CME shares moved in a narrow range, while shares of peers New York Stock Exchange-owner Intercontinental Exchange Inc., Nasdaq Inc. and Cboe Global Markets Inc. nudged higher alongside the broader market.  The exchange\u2019s Globex Futures & Options markets, which handles futures, options, and commodities trading and accounts for 90% of CME Group\u2019s volume, opened at 8:30 a.m. New York time, with trades reported in US futures and options.  Futures and options trading on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange were frozen for several hours due to a data center fault, leaving market participants unable to trade contracts tracking the S&P 500 and multiple other assets.",
